# AI agent rules — shopstack-timesheet

This repository is **Shopstack Timesheet**: a **Next.js (App Router)** app (TypeScript, Tailwind CSS).

## 0. Mandatory: read `doc/` before any implementation

**Do not write or change application code until you have done this.** Skipping is not allowed.

1. Read **[`doc/ai-agent-instruction.md`](../../doc/ai-agent-instruction.md)** in full.
2. Read **every mandatory rule** listed there under `doc/rules/`:
   - `coding.md`, `testing.md`, `lint.md`, `documentation.md`
   - `implementation_completion.md`, `feature-area-documentation.md`
   - `manual_documentation_template.md`
3. Identify the feature area via **[`doc/feature-logic-summary.md`](../../doc/feature-logic-summary.md)**.
4. Read that area under `doc/features/<feature-area>/` in order:
   `README.md` → `domain-features.md` → `feature-logic-summary.md` → relevant `features/*.md`.
5. If those docs are missing for an area you will change, **create the minimum set** per `doc/rules/feature-area-documentation.md` before substantive code changes.

Canonical standards live in **`doc/`**. This Cursor rule enforces that workflow; it does not replace `doc/`.

Team principles: [`doc/README.md`](../../doc/README.md#team-implementation-principles). Session hint: [`doc/prompt.md`](../../doc/prompt.md).

## 1. Core principles

- The AI is an **executor**, not a product owner. Do not invent requirements, business rules, or API contracts.
- Prefer **evidence from feature docs + repo code** (`src/types/`, handlers, lib clients) over assumptions.
- If code and docs disagree, **fix the code or update the docs** explicitly—never leave silent drift.

## 2. Before writing any code

1. Complete **section 0** (read `doc/`).
2. Inspect related **pages** (`src/app/`), **components** (`src/components/`), **API routes** (`src/app/api/`), **lib** (`src/lib/`), and **types** (`src/types/`).
3. Follow **existing patterns** in the same area (Zod validation, `ApiResponse<T>`, `getServerSession(authOptions)`, cached Sheets/Zoho helpers).
4. If behavior changes, update `doc/features/<feature-area>/` (and root setup guides when env/setup changes).

## 3. BFF / server boundary (mandatory)

- **All calls to external APIs** MUST run on the **server**: Route Handlers under `src/app/api/*` or modules under `src/lib/*` used only from the server.
- **Never** call those external APIs from React components or other browser-executed code.
- Client code may call **`/api/*`** (same-origin) only.
- **Secrets and tokens** MUST stay server-side—never in client bundles.

## 4. Architecture boundaries

| Layer | Location | Responsibility |
|--------|-----------|----------------|
| Pages | `src/app/` | Routing and composition |
| Components | `src/components/` | UI and local state. Call `/api/*` only. |
| API routes | `src/app/api/` | Auth-gated handlers; validate; shape `ApiResponse` |
| Lib | `src/lib/` | Server integrations and helpers |
| Contexts | `src/contexts/` | Global client state |
| Types | `src/types/` | Shared domain and API types |
| Middleware | `src/middleware.ts` | Route protection |

## 5. Quality

- Follow `doc/rules/lint.md` and `doc/rules/testing.md`.
- Run **`npx tsc --noEmit`** and **`npm run lint`**; fix new failures before claiming done.
- Completion gate: `doc/rules/implementation_completion.md` and `.cursor/rules/implementation-completion.mdc`.

## 6. Forbidden

- Implementing without reading `doc/ai-agent-instruction.md` and the mandatory `doc/rules/*` files.
- Inventing contracts or business rules without doc or code evidence.
- Calling external APIs from the client or embedding secrets in client code.
- Drive-by large refactors unrelated to the task.
- Completing work while ignoring **new** TypeScript or ESLint failures.
- Copying patterns from other products that do not exist in this repo.

## 7. Final principle

Behave as a **deterministic executor**: read `doc/` → read feature docs → read code → implement minimally → verify types/lint → update docs → report outcomes per `doc/ai-agent-instruction.md` §10.
